From 0aa0642775e117542a770a030a1c283403175524 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ginux-watch-agent <actions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:44:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests(instance): pin instance.id override and unknown-key
 rejection

### What
Pins the `instance.id` override arm: quoted values apply, hostname re-derives, unknown keys and unquoted values fail closed without partial mutation.

### Why it matters
Deleting the arm or making it a no-op silently ignores operator overrides; existing tests pin vcpus/hostname but not id.

### Mutation evidence (fail-then-pass)
| Mutant | Existing suite | New test |
|---|---|---|
| delete `instance.id` arm | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |
| arm parses but discards value | PASS (survives) | FAIL (killed) |

Baseline: PASS. Reproduce: `cargo test -p ginux-instance --lib override_instance_id`.

Prepared with AI assistance; reviewed by me.
---
 crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs b/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs
index d5f17444..1e779b93 100644
--- a/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/ginux-instance/src/lib.rs
@@ -3120,4 +3120,17 @@ failure = "stop"
         c.memory_mib = 15;
         assert!(c.validate().is_err());
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn override_instance_id_and_reject_unknown() {
+        let mut c = InstanceConfig::parse(VALID.as_bytes()).unwrap();
+        c.apply_override(b"instance.id", b"\"other\"").unwrap();
+        assert_eq!(c.id.as_bytes(), b"other");
+        // hostname follows id when unset: override re-derives and validates
+        assert_eq!(c.hostname.as_bytes(), b"other");
+        assert!(c.apply_override(b"instance.nope", b"\"x\"").is_err());
+        // unquoted value is a syntax error, not a silent accept
+        assert!(c.apply_override(b"instance.id", b"bare").is_err());
+        assert_eq!(c.id.as_bytes(), b"other");
+    }
 }
